& [PublishedFrontier]
  + deterministic portable bundle identity no-listener diagnostics and governed disposable initial creation are published and independently verified
  + portable-bundle and bootstrap reentry explicitly leave publisher authenticity trust provisioning supported delivery and production secret lifecycle separately governed
  + no existing signed installer publisher-authenticity production-secret permission repair migration or upgrade specification was found

& [Intent]
  + form the smallest provider-free successor as detached release-signature verification against one supplied public-key policy and the exact current bundle plus evidence bytes
  + preserve policy governance key custody and production publisher authenticity as external claims rather than inferring them from cryptographic verification
  + prove mechanics with fixed public synthetic signing material while shipping no product signing or key-generation command

& [Boundaries]
  + no production key trust-root or secret provisioning signing command installation extraction archive execution current release-binary mutation service provider download remote effect persistence FPGA or Minecraft authority
  + no supported-delivery claim and no policy-governance claim
